+\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The Bonded Commons three-layer architecture. Capability scope (Layer~1) refuses unauthorized actions at the boundary; the evidence chain (Layer~2) records every authorized action in a tamper-evident Merkle structure; the collateral pool (Layer~3) prices authorized-but-harmful actions via posted bonds that pay for damage. The two paths --- \emph  {prevented} (Layer~1 refuses; red dashed) and \emph  {priced} (Layer~1 admits, Layer~3 charges; brass dashed exit) --- together compose defense-in-depth without requiring OS-level isolation. The settlement arrow returns to the principal as refund or slash, depending on whether the evidence chain shows the bonded contract was honoured.}}{7}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
